e focused on other things but  who knows i'm sure the media will tell  us they're doing great  so he went back and found a tweet from  june  where they're talking about lgbtq  equality he said should have focused on  other things  again all i can say is what a scumbag  what an absolute pathetic piece of human  garbage  but that is what the trump family is  that is what donald j trump jr  is  gloating  about what is happening in the country  of afghanistan even though what's  happening in afghanistan is exactly  what his dad wanted done  your dad junior  wanted us to pull all the troops out of  afghanistan  but of course you know he didn't want it  to happen under his administration so  the deal he signed with the taliban  was oh yeah 14 months from now of course  he expected to be president by then and  if he had one of course this would still  be happening  because this is a failure of 20 years of  policy not seven  months  of joe biden  but hey folks there are a couple bright  spots  and one of the bright spots that we're  seeing in the united states today  is that it appears  that the republican party to a tiny tiny  degree  appears to be warming up to the idea  of renewable energy  there was a great op-ed in the hill this  week  where they actually talked about a piece  of legislation  that republicans are pushing in north  carolina without democratic input but  this piece of legislation  would shut down five major coal-fired  power plants in north carolina in the  coming decade cutting carbon dioxide  emissions and improving air quality  importantly the legislation mandates the  maine north carolina utility duke energy  securitize the cost of coal retirements  that provision will save rate payers  from paying the retirement costs of  those facilities  and is something that could be  replicated in other states across the  country to date only a few other states  have adopted a similar policy the bill  would grow renewable energy  substantially by  4700 megawatts